All deliverables are complete. Here is a summary of what was produced and the key correction made:

---

**Critical fix applied:** The original Delphes CMS card does not list the gravitino (PDG 1000039) as invisible. Its default HCAL energy fraction is 1.0, so it deposited all energy in the HCal and appeared as a jet — entirely absent from MET. This was corrected by adding `EnergyFraction {1000039} {0.0}` to both the ECal and HCal calorimeter modules in a patched card (`delphes_card_CMS_gravitino.tcl`). Delphes was re-run with this card; MET mean rose from 205 GeV (broken) to 896 GeV (physical).

**Final results (35.9 fb⁻¹, T5Wg_1750_1700):**

| S_T^γ bin | Yield |
|---|---|
| [600, 800) GeV | 0.327 |
| [800, 1000) GeV | 1.353 |
| [1000, 1300) GeV | 4.066 |
| ≥ 1300 GeV | 34.570 |
| **Total** | **40.3** |

The distribution peaks strongly in the ≥1300 GeV bin, as expected: each NLSP (1700 GeV) → γ + G̃ produces pT(γ) ≈ 850 GeV and pT(G̃) ≈ 850 GeV, so S_T^γ typically falls around 1700 GeV. Weighted selection efficiency (trigger 94.3% × photon ID) is 41.9%.
